WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.630
OT security architecture makes connectivity intentional.

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:08.532
Enterprise IT and control networks should be separated where their functions and risk differ.

00:00:08.532 --> 00:00:11.483
Separation does not mean eliminating every connection.

00:00:11.483 --> 00:00:14.856
It means permitting required communication through controlled, documented,

00:00:14.856 --> 00:00:16.120
and monitored pathways.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.915
An industrial DMZ can buffer enterprise and site operations.

00:00:19.915 --> 00:00:24.552
Services such as jump hosts, remote-access brokers, update repositories, logging gateways,

00:00:24.552 --> 00:00:28.346
and data replication can terminate or mediate cross-boundary activity.

00:00:28.346 --> 00:00:34.249
Enterprise users should not reach controllers directly simply because a route is technically possible.

00:00:34.249 --> 00:00:36.357
Conduits should use least-privilege connectivity.

00:00:36.357 --> 00:00:40.572
Define approved sources, destinations, protocols, direction, business or operational purpose,

00:00:40.572 --> 00:00:41.416
and owner.

00:00:41.416 --> 00:00:43.945
Review administrative traffic, authentication, backup, updates,

00:00:43.945 --> 00:00:47.318
and vendor support as carefully as production data.

00:00:47.318 --> 00:00:49.847
Temporary paths need expiration and removal.

00:00:49.847 --> 00:00:54.063
Monitoring placement should align with trust boundaries and operational value.

00:00:54.063 --> 00:00:57.436
Visibility at enterprise-to-OT boundaries can reveal attempted movement.

00:00:57.436 --> 00:01:02.495
Monitoring within site and control areas can identify unexpected devices, engineering actions,

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:03.760
and unusual communications.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:07.132
Passive techniques may be preferable around sensitive devices.

00:01:07.132 --> 00:01:09.240
Architecture should also preserve resilience.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.878
Understand which functions continue if an enterprise service, DMZ, network link,

00:01:13.878 --> 00:01:15.986
or site server is lost.

00:01:15.986 --> 00:01:17.672
Design local control, redundancy,

00:01:17.672 --> 00:01:23.574
and recovery so a cyber containment decision does not create an avoidable safety problem.

00:01:23.574 --> 00:01:29.055
Modern OT may include cloud analytics, wireless systems, industrial Internet of Things devices,

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:33.271
and vendor-managed services that do not follow a simple hierarchy.

00:01:33.271 --> 00:01:37.487
Extend the architecture with data-flow diagrams, identity paths, external dependencies,

00:01:37.487 --> 00:01:39.173
and current asset records.

00:01:39.173 --> 00:01:42.124
The objective is not a perfect diagram;

00:01:42.124 --> 00:01:46.340
it is controlled communication supported by evidence and operational understanding.
